          "text": "Menstrual cycle pattern and premenstrual symptoms"
        },
        "subject": {
          "reference": "Patient/patient-1"
        },
        "valueString": "Regular 28-day cycles with 5–6 days of moderate bleeding. For years, 7–10 days before menses she experiences marked irritability, mood swings, increased anxiety, and feeling unable to cope. Symptoms resolve 2–3 days after bleeding starts; she feels well and pretty normal mid-cycle."
      }
